From: CrossOver 26.3.0 CXHACK 19488 (dlls/win32u/message.c, peek_message)
Source: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz (sources/wine/dlls/win32u/message.c)
Upstream: no
Why: When a program peeks with exactly PM_REMOVE | PM_QS_INPUT |
 PM_QS_POSTMESSAGE | PM_QS_PAINT | PM_QS_SENDMESSAGE and gets WM_PAINT for
 a WS_EX_COMPOSITED window, send the paint to the window straight away and
 keep looking without PM_QS_PAINT, instead of returning it. Without it,
 such a loop can keep getting WM_PAINT and never see its other messages.
Evidence in 10.0_8: win32u.so's peek_message tests that flag combination,
 WM_PAINT and WS_EX_COMPOSITED, and calls get_window_long and
 send_message_timeout (found by comparing functions, 2026-11-15; it adds no
 strings, so the inventory missed it).
Status: not yet built (2026-11-15).
Applies to: wine 11.21 (macfixes, after 0043)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/message.c b/dlls/win32u/message.c
index de1a484..d9d440b 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/message.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/message.c
@@ -3238,6 +3238,15 @@ static int peek_message( MSG *msg, const struct peek_message_filter *filter )
             {
                 if (!(flags & PM_NOYIELD) && idle_event) NtSetEvent( idle_event, NULL );
             }
+            /* CXHACK 19488 */
+            if (info.msg.message == WM_PAINT &&
+                    flags == (PM_REMOVE | PM_QS_INPUT | PM_QS_POSTMESSAGE | PM_QS_PAINT | PM_QS_SENDMESSAGE) &&
+                    (get_window_long( info.msg.hwnd, GWL_EXSTYLE ) & WS_EX_COMPOSITED ))
+            {
+                send_message( info.msg.hwnd, info.msg.message, info.msg.wParam, info.msg.lParam );
+                flags &= ~PM_QS_PAINT;
+                continue;
+            }
             *msg = info.msg;
             msg->pt = point_phys_to_win_dpi( info.msg.hwnd, info.msg.pt );
             thread_info->message_pos   = MAKELONG( msg->pt.x, msg->pt.y );
